// Contracts tab — FIN site renderer (SkyFund, Session 144, 2026-08-12).
//
// STATIC consumer asset (NOT regenerated by excel_to_dashboard.py), lazy-loaded
// by the inline boot in the tab shell on first activation of #tab-contracts.
//
// WHY THIS EXISTS. Sam is about to start asking vendors for quarterly progress
// against contract deliverables, starting with ASCCC agreement V0718
// ($1,063,900, executed 2025-08-07, expires 2028-06-30). The ask needs somewhere
// to land that is not an inbox.
//
// FIVE RULES IT FOLLOWS — each one earned off the V0718 parse:
//
//  1. AN ABSENT MEASUREMENT IS NOT A ZERO, AND NOT AN ACCUSATION. A reporting
//     period with no row renders "Not recorded", never "Not received". Four
//     quarters closed before this tab existed; it has no knowledge of what was
//     submitted in them, and must not render its own ignorance as vendor
//     delinquency. Same for recorded_count: null is a dash, never 0.
//
//  2. THE CADENCE IS PER-GOAL, AND THE INVOICE CLAUSE OUTRANKS IT. V0718's
//     Evaluation column obliges quarterly check-ins for Goal 1 only — bi-annual
//     for Goal 2, annual for Goal 3. But Section D requires every quarterly
//     invoice to carry a summary of tasks performed FOR EACH DELIVERABLE. So a
//     quarterly ask across all three goals is an existing condition of payment,
//     not a favour. The tab shows both so you always know which you are standing on.
//
//  3. A ROLE DUTY IS NOT A VENDOR DELIVERABLE. Goal 2 lists six bullets that are
//     what an appointed LIAISON does on a campus. ASCCC's obligation is the
//     appointment and the stipend. Scoring the vendor against 115 people's campus
//     work is neither fair nor measurable, so `kind` separates them and only
//     `obligation` rows count toward the goal's progress.
//
//  4. FRACTIONS, NOT CHECKMARKS. The money lives in a handful of countable
//     commitments (115 liaisons, 4 regional leads, 15–30 workgroups), not in the
//     28 rows. Those get their own table with target vs recorded.
//
//  5. A COLLAPSED SECTION STILL INFORMS. Every closed goal header carries its own
//     figures. Open state lives in `state.open`, not the DOM, because render()
//     rewrites innerHTML.
//
// TEAM-GATED (the governance.js / map_users.js posture): vendor payment terms and
// staff contact details are internal working material.
//
// ⚠ DOCUMENTS ARE REVIEWER-ONLY, DELIBERATELY. The 'contract-docs' bucket is
// PRIVATE and its storage RLS is is_allowed_reviewer() with NO team_pass_ok()
// branch — the Storage API does not forward the x-team-pass request header into
// the Postgres session, so a team-phrase user would hit a confusing failure
// rather than a policy denial. The UI says "sign in to open" instead of pretending.
//
// Tests: tests/contracts.test.js
